% Test cases for the seat lift policy (seat_lifts.le): synthetic claims, one
% per criterion of LCD L33801, the benefit points of Policy Article A52518
% and NCD 280.4, and the article's certificate of medical necessity for an
% old claim. Findings are recorded as the treating practitioner's, a medical
% reviewer's or the Council's; a finding nobody made leaves the answer
% conditional. A seat lift mechanism is a purchase: no rental month.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base seat lifts cases includes these resources:
    seat_lifts.

the knowledge base seat lifts cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete claim for an electric seat lift mechanism (E0627): the four
% findings, the type of mechanism, the ordering practitioner, the record of
% the modalities tried, the standard written order, the delivery and its
% proof; a 2026 date of service, so no certificate of medical necessity.
scenario complete is:
    claim 1 is for the seat lift mechanism.
    the HCPCS code of the seat lift mechanism is "E0627".
    the seat lift mechanism is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the finding qualifying seat lift diagnosis about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "severe osteoarthritis of both knees".
    the finding seat lift part of course of treatment about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding completely incapable of standing from any chair about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding able to ambulate once standing about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the seat lift mechanism operates smoothly under the control of the beneficiary.
    the seat lift mechanism effectively assists the beneficiary in standing up and sitting down without other assistance.
    the order for the seat lift mechanism was written by the treating practitioner or a consulting practitioner for the condition.
    the record of the treating practitioner documents that all appropriate therapeutic modalities were tried and failed for Ann.
    the order for the seat lift mechanism is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the seat lift mechanism is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the seat lift mechanism includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the seat lift mechanism includes order date.
    the order for the seat lift mechanism includes description of the item.
    the order for the seat lift mechanism includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the seat lift mechanism includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the seat lift mechanism was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the seat lift mechanism was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the seat lift mechanism.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% A manual mechanism (E0629) for a neuromuscular disease: the other
% qualifying route of criterion 1.
scenario neuromuscular_disease is:
    claim 1 is for the seat lift mechanism.
    the HCPCS code of the seat lift mechanism is "E0629".
    the seat lift mechanism is furnished to Ben.
    the finding qualifying seat lift diagnosis about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "muscular dystrophy".
    the finding seat lift part of course of treatment about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding completely incapable of standing from any chair about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding able to ambulate once standing about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the seat lift mechanism operates smoothly under the control of the beneficiary.
    the seat lift mechanism effectively assists the beneficiary in standing up and sitting down without other assistance.
    the order for the seat lift mechanism was written by the treating practitioner or a consulting practitioner for the condition.
    the record of the treating practitioner documents that all appropriate therapeutic modalities were tried and failed for Ben.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Criterion 1 fails: the medical reviewer finds the arthritis is not severe.
scenario diagnosis_unsupported is:
    claim 1 is for the seat lift mechanism.
    the HCPCS code of the seat lift mechanism is "E0627".
    the seat lift mechanism is furnished to Cy.
    the residence of Cy is private residence.
    the finding qualifying seat lift diagnosis about Cy is unsupported, according to the medical reviewer, because "the record documents mild osteoarthritis of one knee".
    the finding seat lift part of course of treatment about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding completely incapable of standing from any chair about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding able to ambulate once standing about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the seat lift mechanism operates smoothly under the control of the beneficiary.
    the seat lift mechanism effectively assists the beneficiary in standing up and sitting down without other assistance.
    the order for the seat lift mechanism was written by the treating practitioner or a consulting practitioner for the condition.
    the record of the treating practitioner documents that all appropriate therapeutic modalities were tried and failed for Cy.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% Criterion 2 fails: the lift is not part of a course of treatment.
scenario not_course_of_treatment is:
    claim 1 is for the seat lift mechanism.
    the HCPCS code of the seat lift mechanism is "E0627".
    the seat lift mechanism is furnished to Dee.
    the finding qualifying seat lift diagnosis about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "severe osteoarthritis of the hip".
    the finding seat lift part of course of treatment about Dee is unsupported, according to the medical reviewer, because "the lift was requested for convenience and no treatment plan mentions it".
    the finding completely incapable of standing from any chair about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding able to ambulate once standing about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the seat lift mechanism operates smoothly under the control of the beneficiary.
    the seat lift mechanism effectively assists the beneficiary in standing up and sitting down without other assistance.
    the order for the seat lift mechanism was written by the treating practitioner or a consulting practitioner for the condition.
    the record of the treating practitioner documents that all appropriate therapeutic modalities were tried and failed for Dee.
    rn expects answers [].

% Criterion 3 fails: the Council finds the beneficiary rises from an
% armchair of appropriate height — difficulty with a low chair is not enough.
scenario can_stand_council is:
    claim 1 is for the seat lift mechanism.
    the HCPCS code of the seat lift mechanism is "E0627".
    the seat lift mechanism is furnished to Eve.
    the finding qualifying seat lift diagnosis about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "severe osteoarthritis of both knees".
    the finding seat lift part of course of treatment about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding completely incapable of standing from any chair about Eve is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the record shows the beneficiary rising from an armchair of appropriate height with difficulty, which the LCD says is not sufficient justification".
    the finding able to ambulate once standing about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the seat lift mechanism operates smoothly under the control of the beneficiary.
    the seat lift mechanism effectively assists the beneficiary in standing up and sitting down without other assistance.
    the order for the seat lift mechanism was written by the treating practitioner or a consulting practitioner for the condition.
    the record of the treating practitioner documents that all appropriate therapeutic modalities were tried and failed for Eve.
    rn expects answers [].

% Criterion 4 fails: once standing, the beneficiary cannot ambulate.
scenario cannot_ambulate is:
    claim 1 is for the seat lift mechanism.
    the HCPCS code of the seat lift mechanism is "E0627".
    the seat lift mechanism is furnished to Fay.
    the finding qualifying seat lift diagnosis about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "severe osteoarthritis of both hips".
    the finding seat lift part of course of treatment about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding completely incapable of standing from any chair about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding able to ambulate once standing about Fay is unsupported, according to the medical reviewer, because "the beneficiary is transferred by a caregiver to a wheelchair and does not walk".
    the seat lift mechanism operates smoothly under the control of the beneficiary.
    the seat lift mechanism effectively assists the beneficiary in standing up and sitting down without other assistance.
    the order for the seat lift mechanism was written by the treating practitioner or a consulting practitioner for the condition.
    the record of the treating practitioner documents that all appropriate therapeutic modalities were tried and failed for Fay.
    rn expects answers [].

